    "lawCode": "Amd §391-w, Gen Bus L (as proposed in S.9365-A & A.10215-A)",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S777\n\nSPONSOR: FERNANDEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to violations of\nprovisions prohibiting third-party restaurant reservation services from\narranging unauthorized restaurant reservations with food service estab-\nlishments\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2024, c.601, to clarify rulemaking\nprovisions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by removing provisions\nregarding unspecified agency rulemaking.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 601 of the Laws of 2024. S.9365-A and\nA.10215-A both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June\n2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the general business law, in\nrelation to violations of provisions prohibiting third-party restaurant\nreservation services from arranging unauthorized restaurant reservations\nwith food service establishments, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.9365-A and A.10215-A, takes effect.\n",
